Z||000003||88formula||09-21-2000||09:28 PM||||About 200, 228, and 230 HP with a 2.8, 3.1, and 3.4 engine and a Garrett T51 42-3 turbocharger with everything else stock. This was done on Dyno2000. The 3.4 has the most torque.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||09-21-2000||11:07 PM||||Is that rear wheel Hp?  I would think so.  I know that Design One Sytems added a turbo to a 3.4 and he estimates about 275 Hp at the crank at 11 psi (I believe).  Of course he built the 3.4 specifically for the turbo...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||09-22-2000||05:03 PM||||No that is flywheel horsepower with a stock motor. I only did this on a dyno so the figures are only approximate. It shows the stock 2.8 at 134 flywheel horsepower with no turbo, which is almost right on with the factory rating of 135 horsepower.||||reg||1
